# Conditional Logic Engine Specification

## Overview
Conditional logic in forms allows you to create a more responsive and user-friendly experience by tailoring the form to individual user input. It adjusts form content or behavior dynamically based on user responses, showing or hiding fields based on their previous answers.

## Core Conditional Logic Types

### 1. Visibility Conditions (Show/Hide)
This type of conditional logic allows you to show or hide specific fields or question elements based on user responses. It keeps your forms clean and concise, presenting only the relevant information.

```javascript
class VisibilityCondition {
  constructor() {
    this.rules = new Map()
  }
  
  addRule(config) {
    const rule = {
      id: generateId(),
      trigger: {
        fieldId: config.triggerField,
        operator: config.operator, // equals, not_equals, contains, greater_than, etc.
        value: config.triggerValue,
        type: config.triggerType // checkbox, radio, text, number, etc.
      },
      target: {
        fieldIds: config.targetFields,
        action: config.action // 'show', 'hide'
      },
      logic: config.logic || 'AND', // AND/OR for multiple conditions
      priority: config.priority || 0
    }
    
    this.rules.set(rule.id, rule)
    return rule.id
  }
  
  evaluateVisibility(formData) {
    const visibilityMap = new Map()
    
    // Sort rules by priority
    const sortedRules = Array.from(this.rules.values())
      .sort((a, b) => b.priority - a.priority)
    
    for (const rule of sortedRules) {
      const shouldApply = this.evaluateCondition(rule.trigger, formData)
      
      for (const fieldId of rule.target.fieldIds) {
        if (shouldApply) {
          visibilityMap.set(fieldId, rule.target.action === 'show')
        }
      }
    }
    
    return visibilityMap
  }
}
```

### 2. Enable/Disable Conditions
An "Editable If" rule determines whether a specific field is editable based on a specified condition. This rule allows you to dynamically enable or disable the Read-only mode for a survey element.

```javascript
class EnableCondition {
  evaluateEnablement(rule, formData) {
    const triggers = Array.isArray(rule.triggers) ? rule.triggers : [rule.trigger]
    
    // Support complex logic with multiple triggers
    if (rule.logic === 'OR') {
      return triggers.some(trigger => this.checkTrigger(trigger, formData))
    } else { // AND logic
      return triggers.every(trigger => this.checkTrigger(trigger, formData))
    }
  }
  
  checkTrigger(trigger, formData) {
    const fieldValue = formData[trigger.fieldId]
    
    switch (trigger.operator) {
      case 'equals':
        return fieldValue === trigger.value
      case 'not_equals':
        return fieldValue !== trigger.value
      case 'contains':
        return String(fieldValue).includes(trigger.value)
      case 'greater_than':
        return Number(fieldValue) > Number(trigger.value)
      case 'less_than':
        return Number(fieldValue) < Number(trigger.value)
      case 'empty':
        return !fieldValue || fieldValue === ''
      case 'not_empty':
        return fieldValue && fieldValue !== ''
      case 'any_of':
        return Array.isArray(trigger.value) && trigger.value.includes(fieldValue)
      default:
        return false
    }
  }
}
```

### 3. Required Field Conditions
Fields can become required or optional based on other field values.

```javascript
class RequiredCondition {
  evaluateRequired(field, formData, rules) {
    // Default required state
    let isRequired = field.required || false
    
    // Check conditional required rules
    for (const rule of rules) {
      if (rule.targetField === field.id) {
        const triggerValue = formData[rule.triggerField]
        
        if (this.evaluateCondition(rule, triggerValue)) {
          isRequired = rule.makeRequired
        }
      }
    }
    
    return isRequired
  }
}
```

### 4. Value Population Conditions
Automatically populate field values based on other selections.

```javascript
class ValuePopulation {
  populateConditionalValues(rules, formData) {
    const populatedValues = {}
    
    for (const rule of rules) {
      if (rule.type === 'auto_populate') {
        const shouldPopulate = this.evaluateCondition(rule.condition, formData)
        
        if (shouldPopulate) {
          // Support different population strategies
          switch (rule.populationType) {
            case 'static':
              populatedValues[rule.targetField] = rule.value
              break
            
            case 'copy':
              populatedValues[rule.targetField] = formData[rule.sourceField]
              break
            
            case 'calculate':
              populatedValues[rule.targetField] = this.calculate(
                rule.formula,
                formData
              )
              break
            
            case 'lookup':
              populatedValues[rule.targetField] = this.lookupValue(
                rule.lookupTable,
                formData[rule.lookupKey]
              )
              break
          }
        }
      }
    }
    
    return populatedValues
  }
}
```

## Complex Conditional Logic Patterns

### 1. Nested Conditions
Support for conditions that depend on other conditional fields.

```javascript
class NestedConditionEvaluator {
  constructor() {
    this.dependencyGraph = new Map()
  }
  
  buildDependencyGraph(rules) {
    // Build a graph of field dependencies
    for (const rule of rules) {
      const triggers = this.extractTriggerFields(rule)
      const targets = this.extractTargetFields(rule)
      
      for (const target of targets) {
        if (!this.dependencyGraph.has(target)) {
          this.dependencyGraph.set(target, new Set())
        }
        triggers.forEach(trigger => 
          this.dependencyGraph.get(target).add(trigger)
        )
      }
    }
    
    // Check for circular dependencies
    this.validateNoCycles()
  }
  
  evaluateInOrder(formData) {
    // Topological sort to evaluate in dependency order
    const evaluated = new Set()
    const results = {}
    
    const evaluate = (fieldId) => {
      if (evaluated.has(fieldId)) return
      
      // Evaluate dependencies first
      const deps = this.dependencyGraph.get(fieldId) || []
      for (const dep of deps) {
        evaluate(dep)
      }
      
      // Then evaluate this field
      results[fieldId] = this.evaluateField(fieldId, formData, results)
      evaluated.add(fieldId)
    }
    
    // Evaluate all fields
    for (const fieldId of this.dependencyGraph.keys()) {
      evaluate(fieldId)
    }
    
    return results
  }
}
```

### 2. Branching Logic (Page Flow)
Guide responders seamlessly through their journey and direct them to distinct destinations based on their responses.

```javascript
class BranchingLogic {
  constructor() {
    this.branches = new Map()
    this.currentPath = []
  }
  
  defineBranch(config) {
    const branch = {
      id: config.id,
      condition: config.condition,
      nextPage: config.nextPage,
      skipPages: config.skipPages || [],
      customPath: config.customPath || null
    }
    
    this.branches.set(branch.id, branch)
  }
  
  determineNextPage(currentPage, formData) {
    const applicableBranches = this.findApplicableBranches(currentPage, formData)
    
    if (applicableBranches.length === 0) {
      // Default: go to next sequential page
      return this.getNextSequentialPage(currentPage)
    }
    
    // Use highest priority branch
    const branch = applicableBranches[0]
    this.currentPath.push({
      from: currentPage,
      to: branch.nextPage,
      branch: branch.id
    })
    
    return branch.nextPage
  }
  
  generateFormPath(formData) {
    // Pre-calculate entire form path based on current data
    const path = []
    let currentPage = 'start'
    
    while (currentPage !== 'end') {
      path.push(currentPage)
      currentPage = this.determineNextPage(currentPage, formData)
    }
    
    return path
  }
}
```

### 3. Cross-Field Validation
Validation rules that involve multiple fields.

```javascript
class CrossFieldValidation {
  addValidationRule(rule) {
    return {
      id: rule.id,
      fields: rule.fields, // Array of field IDs involved
      validator: rule.validator, // Function that validates
      message: rule.message,
      severity: rule.severity || 'error' // error, warning, info
    }
  }
  
  validateDateRange(startFieldId, endFieldId) {
    return {
      fields: [startFieldId, endFieldId],
      validator: (formData) => {
        const start = new Date(formData[startFieldId])
        const end = new Date(formData[endFieldId])
        return start <= end
      },
      message: 'End date must be after start date',
      severity: 'error'
    }
  }
  
  validateTotalPercentage(fieldIds) {
    return {
      fields: fieldIds,
      validator: (formData) => {
        const total = fieldIds.reduce((sum, id) => 
          sum + (Number(formData[id]) || 0), 0
        )
        return Math.abs(total - 100) < 0.01 // Allow for floating point errors
      },
      message: 'Percentages must total 100%',
      severity: 'error'
    }
  }
}
```

## Visual Conditional Logic Builder

```javascript
class VisualLogicBuilder {
  constructor() {
    this.canvas = null
    this.nodes = [] // Field nodes
    this.connections = [] // Logic connections
  }
  
  renderVisualBuilder() {
    return {
      type: 'canvas',
      elements: [
        this.renderFieldNodes(),
        this.renderLogicConnections(),
        this.renderConditionLabels()
      ],
      interactions: {
        onNodeClick: this.handleNodeClick,
        onConnectionDrag: this.handleConnectionDrag,
        onConditionEdit: this.handleConditionEdit
      }
    }
  }
  
  generateRuleFromVisual() {
    // Convert visual representation to executable rules
    const rules = []
    
    for (const connection of this.connections) {
      rules.push({
        trigger: {
          fieldId: connection.source.id,
          operator: connection.condition.operator,
          value: connection.condition.value
        },
        target: {
          fieldId: connection.target.id,
          action: connection.action
        }
      })
    }
    
    return rules
  }
  
  validateLogicFlow() {
    // Check for issues in the logic flow
    const issues = []
    
    // Check for circular dependencies
    if (this.hasCircularDependency()) {
      issues.push({
        type: 'error',
        message: 'Circular dependency detected'
      })
    }
    
    // Check for unreachable fields
    const unreachable = this.findUnreachableFields()
    if (unreachable.length > 0) {
      issues.push({
        type: 'warning',
        message: `Fields may be unreachable: ${unreachable.join(', ')}`
      })
    }
    
    return issues
  }
}
```

## Performance Optimization

```javascript
class ConditionalLogicOptimizer {
  constructor() {
    this.ruleCache = new Map()
    this.evaluationCache = new Map()
  }
  
  optimizeRules(rules) {
    // Group rules by trigger field for efficient evaluation
    const optimized = {
      byTriggerField: new Map(),
      byTargetField: new Map(),
      globalRules: []
    }
    
    for (const rule of rules) {
      // Index by trigger field
      if (rule.trigger?.fieldId) {
        if (!optimized.byTriggerField.has(rule.trigger.fieldId)) {
          optimized.byTriggerField.set(rule.trigger.fieldId, [])
        }
        optimized.byTriggerField.get(rule.trigger.fieldId).push(rule)
      }
      
      // Index by target field
      for (const targetId of rule.target?.fieldIds || []) {
        if (!optimized.byTargetField.has(targetId)) {
          optimized.byTargetField.set(targetId, [])
        }
        optimized.byTargetField.get(targetId).push(rule)
      }
    }
    
    return optimized
  }
  
  memoizedEvaluate(rule, formData) {
    const cacheKey = `${rule.id}_${JSON.stringify(formData)}`
    
    if (this.evaluationCache.has(cacheKey)) {
      return this.evaluationCache.get(cacheKey)
    }
    
    const result = this.evaluateRule(rule, formData)
    this.evaluationCache.set(cacheKey, result)
    
    // Limit cache size
    if (this.evaluationCache.size > 1000) {
      const firstKey = this.evaluationCache.keys().next().value
      this.evaluationCache.delete(firstKey)
    }
    
    return result
  }
}
```

## Best Practices

### Design Principles
1. **Keep logic intuitive** - Users should understand why fields appear/disappear
2. **Avoid overcomplication** - Too many conditions confuse users
3. **Test thoroughly** - Conditional logic can create complex paths
4. **Provide clear feedback** - Explain why fields are disabled/hidden
5. **Handle edge cases** - What happens when conditions conflict?

### Implementation Guidelines
1. **Evaluate conditions efficiently** - Cache results, optimize rule order
2. **Handle circular dependencies** - Detect and prevent infinite loops
3. **Support undo/redo** - Users may change answers that trigger conditions
4. **Maintain accessibility** - Screen readers must announce changes
5. **Test all paths** - Ensure every combination works correctly

### Performance Considerations
1. **Batch DOM updates** - Don't update fields one at a time
2. **Use requestAnimationFrame** - For smooth animations
3. **Debounce evaluations** - Don't re-evaluate on every keystroke
4. **Lazy evaluate** - Only check rules for changed fields
5. **Optimize rule storage** - Index by trigger and target fields

